   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### The 6×6 FSoV scalar product against the vacuum at a second twist $w$\n\nLeft state: $\\Omega=e_1\\otimes e_1$ of the chain with twist $\\mathrm{diag}(w_1,w_2,w_3)$ (unimodular); its dual $Q^j_w(u)=w_j^{-u/h}q^j_w(u)$, $\\deg q^j_w=2\\lambda_j$, from the dual Baxter equation with $\\Omega$'s eigenvalues at twist $w$. Right state: $\\Psi_B$ of the $z$-chain. The $6\\times6$ is that of `L2-mathcalA.wb` (one contour around all poles $\\theta_s+nh$, rows $(\\alpha,i,j)$, columns $u^\\beta\\{-Q^jQ_i,\\ Q^jQ_i^{[-2]},\\ Q^{j[2]}Q_i\\}$), divided by $\\Psi^{\\rm ref}_B$. Fit $V$ with $V\\cdot\\Psi_B=S_B$ and test whether $V=C\\,(u\\otimes u)$, $u=e_1^Te^{aE_{12}}e^{bE_{13}}e^{cE_{23}}$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 7. Vacuum at twist w: dual Q's, 6x6 FSoV det against every Psi_B, fitted covector V(w), rotation test.\n   V is reshaped as a dsT x dsT matrix M[n1, n2] (row-major = E1T/E2T ordering). A global rotation (e1 g) (x) (e1 g) is exactly\n   M = C u u^T: rank 1 and symmetric, with u in the orbit of e1^T. ---- *)\nClearAll[wW, tcoefW, tauW, omW, qdW, QuW, polesV, wPoleV, perV, rowKeysV, colKeysV, blockV, detW, psiRefV, sW, vW, matOf, rotTest, uOf, abcFit];\nwW = {3/2, 5/4, 8/15};\ntcoefW[a_, k_] := Sum[(Times @@ wW[[II]]) N[qcoefT[II, k], precT], {II, Subsets[Range[3], {a}]}];\nomW = UnitVector[dcT, 1];\ntauW = Table[Sum[(tcoefW[a, k] . omW)[[1]] u^k, {k, 0, 2 a}], {a, 3}];\nqdW = Table[solveMonicT[BaxDualT[tauW, 1 / N[wW[[j]], precT]], 2 repT[[j]]], {j, 3}];\nQuW[j_, x_] := N[wW[[j]], precT]^(-x / hT) qpolyT[qdW[[j, 1]], x];\n\npolesV = Flatten @ Table[thT[[s]] + n hT, {s, 2}, {n, repT[[3]], repT[[1]]}];\nwPoleV = Table[1 / Times @@ (polesV[[r]] - Delete[polesV, r]), {r, Length[polesV]}];\nperV[alpha_, x_] := Exp[2 Pi I (alpha - 1) SetPrecision[x, precT] / hT];\nrowKeysV = Flatten[Table[{alpha, ij}, {alpha, 2}, {ij, {{1, 3}, {1, 2}, {2, 3}}}], 1];\ncolKeysV = Flatten[Table[{beta, st}, {beta, 0, 1}, {st, 3}], 1];\n(* each entry is a list over B *)\nblockV[{alpha_, {i_, j_}}, {beta_, st_}] := Sum[\n    With[{x = polesV[[r]]}, wPoleV[[r]] perV[alpha, x] x^beta Switch[st,\n        1, -QuW[j, x] Table[QdT[B, i, x], {B, dcT}],\n        2, QuW[j, x] Table[QdT[B, i, x - hT], {B, dcT}],\n        3, QuW[j, x + hT] Table[QdT[B, i, x], {B, dcT}]]],\n    {r, Length[polesV]}];\ndetW = Module[{blocks = Table[blockV[rk, ck], {rk, rowKeysV}, {ck, colKeysV}]}, Table[Det[blocks[[All, All, B]]], {B, dcT}]];\npsiRefV = Table[Product[QdT[B, 1, th + repT[[2]] hT] (QdT[B, 1, th] QdT[B, 2, th - hT] - QdT[B, 2, th] QdT[B, 1, th - hT]), {th, thT}], {B, dcT}];\nsW = detW / psiRefV;\nvW = sW . Inverse[ketMatT];\n\nmatOf[v_] := Partition[v, dsT];\n(* {sigma2/sigma1 of M, |M - M^T|/|M|} *)\nrotTest[v_] := With[{M = matOf[v]}, With[{sv = SingularValueList[N[M, 30], 2]}, {If[Length[sv] < 2, 0, sv[[2]] / sv[[1]]], Max[Abs[M - Transpose[M]]] / Max[Abs[M]]}]];\nuOf[v_] := matOf[v][[1]] / matOf[v][[1, 1]];\n(* fit u = e1^T e^{a E12} e^{b E13} e^{c E23} by least squares over all components (it is polynomial in a, b, c) *)\nabcFit[uu_] := Module[{uS, sol, a, b, c},\n    uS = UnitVector[dsT, 1] . MatrixExp[a Normal[ElT[1, 2]]] . MatrixExp[b Normal[ElT[1, 3]]] . MatrixExp[c Normal[ElT[2, 3]]];\n    sol = FindRoot[Evaluate[Thread[(uS - uu)[[Flatten @ Position[Normal @ Abs[uS /. {a -> 1/3, b -> 1/5, c -> 1/7}], _?(# > 0 &)][[2 ;; 4]]]] == 0]], {{a, 1/2}, {b, 1/2}, {c, 1/2}}, WorkingPrecision -> 60, MaxIterations -> 500];\n    {{a, b, c} /. sol, Max[Abs[(uS /. sol) - uu]]}\n];\n\nGrid[\n    {\n        {\"w (unimodular)\", {wW, Times @@ wW}},\n        {\"Omega eigen residual at twist w\", N[Max[Table[Max[Abs[tcoefW[a, k] . omW - Coefficient[tauW[[a]], u, k] omW]], {a, 3}, {k, 0, 2 a}]], 3]},\n        {\"dual Baxter residuals of the w-vacuum\", N[qdW[[All, 2]], 3]},\n        {\"min |det_B|, max |det_B|\", N[{Min[Abs[detW]], Max[Abs[detW]]}, 3]},\n        {\"V: sigma2/sigma1, asymmetry of M\", N[rotTest[vW], 3]},\n        {\"u = row 1 of M / M11; fit (a, b, c), residual\", N[abcFit[uOf[vW]], 12]}\n    },\n    Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left\n]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"389651\" data-output-id=\"37\" data-out-n=\"555\" data-sub-idx=\"25\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"9\" data-sub-start=\"39\" data-sub-end=\"49\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[555]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"22\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:7.29em;vertical-align:-3.375em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.915em;\"><span style=\"top:-5.875em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.875em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:7.25em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-3.375em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.875em;\"><span style=\"top:-6.025em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">w (unimodular)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.825em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">Omega eigen residual at twist w</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.615em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">dual Baxter residuals of the w-vacuum</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top: