  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 9. Is u(w) a vacL rotation? vacL(y) = e1^T e^{p1 E12} e^{p2 E13} e^{p3 E23} with p3 = p2 (y3 - y1)/(p1 (y2 - y3)); as a flag this is the single\n   condition incid(flag, y) = y1 l1 pi23 - y2 l2 pi13 + y3 l3 pi12 = 0 (invariant under y -> alpha y + beta). y = (1,1,1) is plain incidence.\n   Exact, from the rationalized fit of u(w). ---- *)\nClearAll[incid];\nincid[{l_, pp_}, y_] := y[[1]] l[[1]] pp[[3]] - y[[2]] l[[2]] pp[[2]] + y[[3]] l[[3]] pp[[1]];\nGrid[\n    Prepend[\n        Table[With[{fl = flag[Rationalize[abcFit[uOf[vOfW[ww]]][[1]], 10^-40]]},\n            {ww, incid[fl, {1, 1, 1}], incid[fl, zT], incid[fl, 1 / (zT - ww[[2]])], incid[fl, 1 / (zT - ww[[3]])], incid[fl, 1 / (zT - ww[[1]])]}], {ww, wListV}],\n        {\"w\", \"flag (y = 1)\", \"vacL relation, y = z\", \"y = 1/(z - w2)\", \"y = 1/(z - w3)\", \"y = 1/(z - w1)\"}\n    ],\n    Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left\n]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
